&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blend is a diverse team of problem solvers who believe that the world’s financial resources should be more accessible. Our cloud banking platform is used by Wells Fargo, U.S. Bank, and over 330 other financial services firms to acquire more customers, increase productivity, and deliver end-to-end digital experiences. Our software enables our customers to process an average of more than $5 billion in loans per day, making it possible for consumers to reach their financial goals faster and lead better lives. Come do work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Business Automation Engineer&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Business Automation Engineer, you’ll partner with teams across the company to rethink and refactor how work gets done. You’ll find manual and repetitive processes and then design and build automations to improve the quality of work and day-to-day business life of our internal partners. We’re focused on deploying efficient and adaptable automations that actually solve problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As one of the first members of the team, you’ll help build the foundation for a scalable hub of automations and integrations, using both off-the-shelf products and custom code where appropriate. You’ll help shape the workflows that make our team an effective and reliable partner for bringing business processes into an automated, AI-augmented world. You’ll work closely with security and IT leadership from the beginning to ensure the team’s foundations and, therefore, the rest of the company’s internal automation efforts are secure, auditable, and built to last.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How You’ll Contribute&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business stakeholder to understand workflows and triage high-impact automation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business, build, and deploy automations across various SaaS tooling, internal systems, and APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI and agentic patterns when it adds value to business operations workflows and recognize when simpler, more deterministic solutions are the better choice.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build with a secure-by-default mindset, including the incorporation of access controls, secrets management, logging, and the proper handling of sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish team patterns and culture, including documentation, testing, and ongoing operational maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be willing to tinker, iterate, and improve existing systems as we gain more context and mastery over the business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Are&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience building integrations, internal tooling, or automations in a business or operations setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in at least one scripting language (Python, Javascript, or similar) and/or a general purpose programming language (Typescript, Go, Rust, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevOps-minded engineer familiar with infrastructure-as-code tools (Ansible, Terraform, GitHub Actions, containers, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building with LLMs and creating agentic workflows (prompting, tool use and curation, benchmarking evaluations, guardrails, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with workflow or integration platforms (Workato, Zapier, n8n, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and pragmatic. Able to translate business processes into effective automations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP) and serverless or containerized deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with common business systems, such as NetSuite, Salesforce, Workday, Freshservice, and HR tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in security, compliance, or working within a regulated or controlled environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range:&lt;/strong&gt; $124,000 – $145,000 (This applies to full time hires. Final offer determined by multiple factors, including but not limited to function, level, geographic location, job related knowledge, skills, and experience.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus (if applicable):&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Eligibility is contingent upon both company performance against established goals and achievement of individual performance objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity :&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Meaningful Restricted Stock Units in public company stock (NYSE: BLND) so you share in Blend’s long-term growth and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits at a Glance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a comprehensive and competitive benefits package designed to support your health and work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer medical, dental, and vision benefits, with a generous employer contribution that helps keep your medical insurance costs low.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid life, short-term, and long-term disability coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO, holidays, and maternity/parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP): mental health, legal, childcare &amp;amp; eldercare, financial planning, college search, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary benefits: accident, critical illness, hospital indemnity, identity theft, and legal insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly wellness stipend for fitness, mental health, and well-being&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional perks: Milk Stork, pet insurance, and paid volunteer time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Future&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) retirement plan with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax savings: healthcare &amp;amp; dependent care FSAs, Limited Purpose FSA, and HSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blend is a diverse team of problem solvers who believe that the world’s financial resources should be more accessible. Our cloud banking platform is used by Wells Fargo, U.S. Bank, and over 330 other financial services firms to acquire more customers, increase productivity, and deliver end-to-end digital experiences. Our software enables our customers to process an average of more than $5 billion in loans per day, making it possible for consumers to reach their financial goals faster and lead better lives. Come do work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Client Sales Executive-Named Accounts &lt;/strong&gt;is the strategic quarterback for Blend’s top-tier financial institution customers who are some of the largest banks and credit unions in the US. In this role, you’ll own the overall relationship with an assigned list of banks and credit unions who are 20B+ in AUM - driving expansion, retention, and executive alignment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Client Sales - Named Accounts&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Customer Success, Support, and Consulting to ensure customers realize the full value of their partnership with Blend. You’ll define and execute a long-term account strategy, align on customer goals and success metrics, and identify new opportunities to drive meaningful growth - for both our clients and Blend. This is a high-impact, highly visible role for a strategic, customer-obsessed sales leader who thrives on building trust, shaping strategy, and delivering measurable outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account Strategy &amp;amp; Expansion (50%)&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute account strategies to drive revenue growth, targeting 10-15%annual expansion (e.g., additional licenses, premium modules).
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and Plan Renewal Strategies designed to uplift PFL, drive revenue and encourage Blend usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize the selling of partner products that are part of the overall blend ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify cross-sell/upsell opportunities in collaboration with Senior Professional Services Consultant, using customization and adoption insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs) with executive stakeholders, presenting ROI and strategic roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Management (30%)&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain C-level relationships with client executives, ensuring alignment on business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the escalation point for strategic issues (e.g., major compliance disputes, contract renewals).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Coordination (15%)&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Senior Professional Services Consultant and Training &amp;amp; Enablement Specialist to align on customization needs, feature adoption, metrics, and training outcomes.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and Expand Annual Services Spend/ P&amp;amp;L.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the centralized due diligence team for executive-level TPRM/due diligence escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting (5%)&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain CRM updates (e.g., Salesforce) on account health, opportunities, and risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track expansion metrics and retention rates for leadership reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10 years in account management or sales in SaaS/fintech, with a proven track record of managing enterprise-level accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving expansion for financial institutions, ideally with SaaS or low-code platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ideal candidates have experience selling loan origination software, digital account opening, digital lending, mortgage focused solutions and have experience working with Top 50 Banks and or Credit Unions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic account planning and revenue growth expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional executive communication and negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in CRM tools (e.g., Salesforce) and QBR preparation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize customization and adoption data for strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, or related field; MBA preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker with a customer-centric mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership and ability to navigate complex stakeholder dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Blend, we are committed to offering a competitive compensation package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To comply with local legislation, as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base pay ranges on all job postings regardless of desired hiring location. Final base pay offer amounts will vary depending on multiple factors, including but not limited to function, level, geographic location, job related knowledge, skills, and experience. Beyond base pay, Blends benefits and perks are described below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range:&lt;/strong&gt; $125,000 and $150,000 (OTE includes base + variable with a 50/50 split. This applies to full time hires. Final offer determined by multiple factors, including but not limited to function, level, geographic location, job related knowledge, skills, and experience.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity :&lt;/strong&gt; Meaningful Restricted Stock Units in public company stock (NYSE: BLND) so you share in Blend’s long-term growth and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits at a Glance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a comprehensive and competitive benefits package designed to support your health and work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer medical, dental, and vision benefits, with a generous employer contribution that helps keep your medical insurance costs low.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid life, short-term, and long-term disability coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO, holidays, and maternity/parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP): mental health, legal, childcare &amp;amp; eldercare, financial planning, college search, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary benefits: accident, critical illness, hospital indemnity, identity theft, and legal insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly wellness stipend for fitness, mental health, and well-being&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional perks: Milk Stork, pet insurance, and paid volunteer time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Future&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) retirement plan with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax savings: healthcare &amp;amp; dependent care FSAs, Limited Purpose FSA, and HSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blend is a diverse team of problem solvers who believe that the world’s financial resources should be more accessible. Our cloud banking platform is used by Wells Fargo, U.S. Bank, and over 330 other financial services firms to acquire more customers, increase productivity, and deliver end-to-end digital experiences. Our software enables our customers to process an average of more than $5 billion in loans per day, making it possible for consumers to reach their financial goals faster and lead better lives. Come do work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Professional Services Consultant at Blend, you understand Blend’s platform and the client’s needs to help deliver a solution that exceeds expectations. You work with teams from across the company to rapidly implement and improve our product offerings, providing project leadership and configuration expertise on Blend’s products. The ideal candidate is excited to work both independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, highly visible role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You project-manage the deployment for your engagements: you plan the work, configure the product, manage dependencies and risk, secure sign-offs, and act as the primary client contact through go-live. You present in person and remotely to explain how Blend products work and how they should be implemented, and you translate client needs into clear written requirements for Product Owners and the technical integration teams. You are comfortable navigating ambiguity and juggling multiple engagements at once. As you grow in the role, you take on more complex, higher-risk engagements, become a go-to expert for a product or domain, and raise the bar for other consultants. Similar titles include Deployment Lead, Implementation Consultant, Technical Project Manager, and Professional Services Lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll contribute&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn and master Blend products&lt;/strong&gt; in order to tackle customer business challenges as the configuration and implementation lead, working toward product certification and being able to demo Blend against real use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the engagement end-to-end:&lt;/strong&gt; develop and maintain project plans, forecast dates, integrate customer testing schedules into the implementation plan, track progress, manage dependencies, risks, and issues, and own delivery to schedule and budget while flagging and escalating critical risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Present in person and remotely&lt;/strong&gt; to customer business and technical stakeholders to explain how Blend products work and how they should be implemented, running demos, walkthroughs, and working sessions that keep the engagement aligned. Occasional onsite travel to client locations is expected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with lender business and technical resources to &lt;strong&gt;produce business requirements and functional design documents,&lt;/strong&gt; and partner with customer business teams to understand business objectives and integration requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate client needs&lt;/strong&gt; into clear, comprehensive written requirements and specifications for Product Owners and the technical integration teams, so product and engineering can build and integrate against a precise, unambiguous scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete and manage &lt;strong&gt;end-to-end software and platform configuration&lt;/strong&gt; changes based on client requirements, from screens and application settings to branding and environment changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute &lt;strong&gt;integration testing&lt;/strong&gt; and user acceptance testing of customer implementations, triage and troubleshoot defects, and run &lt;strong&gt;launch activities to a successful go-live.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Blend Product and Engineering teams to share customer requirements, &lt;strong&gt;influence product priorities&lt;/strong&gt;, and further improve Blend core product features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the &lt;strong&gt;engagement manager and primary client contact&lt;/strong&gt; for your accounts, running regular meetings, leading discovery, recommending concrete solution options within known patterns, and owning customer satisfaction. As scope grows, structure ambiguous client asks into clear requirements and negotiate trade-offs across timeline, complexity, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience with full-lifecycle package software implementations (SaaS preferred). Candidates with broader experience will own multiple, more complex, higher-risk engagements and act as a subject-matter expert.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to project-manage an engagement, running multiple projects at once, including project plan preparation and maintenance, scope control, and project risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to speak with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, present in person and remotely, explain how products work and should be implemented, and tailor the message to each audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at writing clear requirements and specifications for Product Owners and technical integration teams, translating business needs into precise, buildable scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail with clear, logical thinking, ensuring configurations, requirements, and plans are accurate and complete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on technical configuration experience, such as screens and user interface, application settings or parameters, and branding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic to intermediate software development experience, with familiarity with software programming principles and logic-based structures; working knowledge of Velocity is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business analysis experience across process design, requirements gathering, and synthesis; Green Belt, Six Sigma, or similar training is a nice to have.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of JSON and APIs, with the ability to troubleshoot integrations and collaborate with Product and Engineering teams for resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to propose creative technical solutions to challenging problems and to communicate technical concepts and specifications clearly and efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong personal initiative and drive to execute with minimal oversight, and experience working in a multifaceted environment wearing many hats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Banking or finance industry experience is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Blend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in the United States. You will partner closely with US-based clients and teams, operating in US time zones. Occasional travel to client sites is expected as part of the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range:&lt;/strong&gt; $109,000 – $128,000 (This applies to full time hires. Final offer determined by multiple factors, including but not limited to function, level, geographic location, job related knowledge, skills, and experience.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus (if applicable):&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Eligibility is contingent upon both company performance against established goals and achievement of individual performance objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity :&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Meaningful Restricted Stock Units in public company stock (NYSE: BLND) so you share in Blend’s long-term growth and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits at a Glance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a comprehensive and competitive benefits package designed to support your health and work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer medical, dental, and vision benefits, with a generous employer contribution that helps keep your medical insurance costs low.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid life, short-term, and long-term disability coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO, holidays, and maternity/parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP): mental health, legal, childcare &amp;amp; eldercare, financial planning, college search, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary benefits: accident, critical illness, hospital indemnity, identity theft, and legal insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly wellness stipend for fitness, mental health, and well-being&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional perks: Milk Stork, pet insurance, and paid volunteer time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Future&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) retirement plan with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax savings: healthcare &amp;amp; dependent care FSAs, Limited Purpose FSA, and HSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blend is a diverse team of problem solvers who believe that the world’s financial resources should be more accessible. Our cloud banking platform is used by Wells Fargo, U.S. Bank, and over 330 other financial services firms to acquire more customers, increase productivity, and deliver end-to-end digital experiences. Our software enables our customers to process an average of more than $5 billion in loans per day, making it possible for consumers to reach their financial goals faster and lead better lives. Come do work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blend is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Director of Revenue Accounting &lt;/strong&gt;to lead and scale the revenue recognition and billing and collections functions. This leader will be responsible for overseeing the end-to-end quote-to-cash process, managing a growing team, leading audit support, and partnering cross-functionally to ensure streamlined contract processing and billing workflows. The ideal candidate brings a deep understanding of complex SaaS revenue models, a strong technical accounting background specifically with ASC 606, a passion for automation and process optimization, and experience leading high-performance teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Contribute:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Company’s revenue accounting function, ensuring compliance with ASC 606.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical accounting assessments of customer contracts, with the focus on non-standard terms, contract modifications, and multi-element arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and evolve the Company’s revenue recognition policies and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure SOX 404(b) compliant controls are documented and operating effectively across all quote-to-cash processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary contact for internal and external audits related to revenue and receivables, including providing audit deliverables and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead process transformation initiatives to automate and streamline workflows, including an AI roadmap for revenue accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Deal Desk, Sales, Legal and FP&amp;amp;A to enable timely, compliant, and scalable contracting and revenue processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, and Deployment teams to assess impacts of new offerings on revenue recognition and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the completeness and accuracy of transaction data that drives billing and revenue, spanning across platform volume, customer-reported usage, and partner data - including the controls, reconciliations, and cross-functional collaboration that goes with it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage updates to Blend’s standalone selling price analysis and transaction price allocation methodologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the billings and collections function, ensuring accurate, timely, and complete invoicing and cash application, and own the reporting that comes out of it — AR aging and reserves, unbilled and deferred revenue balances, and collections metrics such as DSO.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide monthly and quarterly revenue close processes, overseeing revenue recognition entries, flux analysis, internal reporting, and external revenue-related disclosures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and mentor a team of revenue and billing professionals with a focus on professional growth and high performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
